        <mxCell id="MoNfp9eKUkRgfcgZ35LG-280" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=1;rounded=0;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;strokeColor=#0000FF;" edge="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="-409" y="1387.07" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="-379" y="1107.07" as="targetPoint" />
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="-430" y="1387.07" />
              <mxPoint x="-429.75" y="1108.83" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MoNfp9eKUkRgfcgZ35LG-281" value="&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;Solar panel&#39;s negative connects to a negative bus, its positive connects to a fuse, Fuse to schottley diode, diode to XL4016 8A buck converter positive input. negative of XL4016 buck connects to the same negative bus, output positive of te XL4016 buck converter connets to a positive bus, while its output negative is left not connected to anything beause it is internally already connected to the negative bus. The BMS (10A) positive connects to the same positive bus while its negative connects to INA226 shunt (resistor) sensor which the connects to the same negative bus. The positive of the battery connects to the positive bus (same terminal with positive BMS), while the negative of the battery connects to the B- terminal of the BMS. LM2596 buck converter input positive connects to the positive bus (via a fuse and a relay) while its negative connects to the the common negative bus. The positive and negative of one bulbs connect to the output of the LM2596 output positiv and negative respectively (set to deliver 5v as output). second LM2596 buck converter input positive connects to the positive bus (via a fuse and a relay) while its negative connects to the the common negative bus. The positive and negative of second bulbs connects to the output of the LM2596 output positive and negative respectively (set to deliver 5v as output)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;The positive of a USB module (3A) connects to the positive bus (via a fuse and a relay), there will be x 3 of such USB module so 3 phones can charge.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;LM2596 buck converter input positive connects to the positive bus (via a fuse) while its negative connects to the the common negative bus. The ESP32 connects to this buck converter. The INA226 is not a digital-pin sensor. It uses I2C, so SDA and SCL connect to the ESP32 I2C pins (GPIO 21 and 22 by default), and VCC and GND to the 5 V (or 3.3 V) rail and ground.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The relays are driven by ESP32 GPIO pins, usually through the relay module’s input pins. The relay module’s coils run from the 5 V rail. Check whether the module is active-low or active-high.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For the total-load shunt to read correctly, every load negative must return through it. That means a separate “load ground” node:&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Load negatives (fan, bulb bucks, USB buck, ESP32 buck) → load shunt → negative bus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;The 12v fan&#39;s positive connect to the positive bus (via a fuse and a relay) while its negative connects to the common negative bus.&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=13;labelBorderColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="120" y="785.5" width="460" height="422.51" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MoNfp9eKUkRgfcgZ35LG-282" value="" style="shape=process;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;rotation=0;strokeWidth=2;size=0.21212121212121213;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-236.66" y="1103.7099999999998" width="39" height="18.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
